# 13. IIT is misstated

IIT does not simply say:

[
\Phi=\text{consciousness}.
]

Its mature versions identify experience with a maximally irreducible cause–effect structure, not a single scalar (\Phi). (\Phi) measures aspects of irreducibility but is not by itself the complete qualitative structure of experience.

More importantly, IIT’s identity claim is one proposed bridge:

[
\text{intrinsic causal structure}
=================================

\text{experience}.
]

It is not an independently proven result. The 2025 adversarial study challenged central biological predictions associated with both IIT and GNWT and did not establish either as the correct theory. ([Nature][4])

So IIT supports the legitimacy of identity-style explanations:

[
X\text{ is consciousness},
]

but it does not validate your particular identity:

[
\text{self-maintaining significance}
====================================

\text{consciousness}.
]

